 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The agreement rule with direct pronouns",
     "texto": [
      "Normally, with **avere** the past participle ends in neutral **-o**: **Ho comprato la pasta**. But if you replace «la pasta» with the direct pronoun **la**, the past participle must agree in gender and number: **L'ho comprata**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Contracted forms and plural",
     "texto": [
      "**Lo** and **la** are compulsorily elided before «ho, hai, ha, abbiamo, avete, hanno»: **L'ho visto** (I've seen it), **L'ho vista** (I've seen her).",
      "By contrast, the plurals **li** and **le** are NEVER elided: **Li ho visti** (I've seen them, masculine), **Le ho viste** (I've seen them, feminine)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Direct pronoun with passato prossimo",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Question with noun",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Answer with pronoun",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
